From 840683d96f2ba4bf17d2ece70debd3cc03434646 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:18:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] CuDSSSolver: direct solver of NVIDIA on the GPU in the
 factory

The factory of linear solvers gains the solver CuDSSSolver (parallel, MFEM
built with cuDSS), with the parameters Symmetric, PositiveDefinite (the
symmetric modes read the lower triangle of the matrices, as MUMPS) and
ReuseAnalysis. It is refused without a device on a CUDA GPU, cuDSS reading
the matrices and the vectors on the device.

mfem::CuDSSSolver (MFEM 4.10) stops the program when given a matrix whose
size differs from the one of the previous matrix, and the reuse of its
analysis is chosen before its first matrix, after which only the number of
coefficients of the next matrices is checked. The solver of the factory,
internals::CuDSSDirectSolver, creates a new mfem::CuDSSSolver when the size
of the matrix changes and, with ReuseAnalysis, when its pattern changed on
one process.

The comparison of the patterns of the parallel matrices of hypre is moved
to an internal unit, HypreMatrixPattern, shared by the MUMPS and cuDSS
solvers. The function getNumberOfMUMPSAnalyses becomes getNumberOfAnalyses
and covers both solvers. The test MUMPSReuseAnalysisTest becomes
DirectSolverReuseAnalysisTest, with an option --solver, the refusal of
cuDSS without GPU and cuDSS variants on the GPU on one and two processes.
The distributed analysis of cuDSS 0.7.1 fails when some rows only have a
diagonal entry (observed with two processes on one GPU): these steps of
the test are skipped for cuDSS on several processes; the tangent operators
of mfem-mgis keep the entries of the rows of the imposed degrees of
freedom.

On the elasticity matrix of ex8 of mfem-mgis-examples (28548 unknowns,
one process), a factorization takes 0.018 s with cuDSS (symmetric
positive definite, analysis reused) instead of 0.203 s with MUMPS on the
host (analysis reused), and ex8 on the GPU takes 4.4 s instead of 9.8 s.
